<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Estonia (1561-1721)</h1><p class="st-meta">1561 CE – 1721 CE · capital Reval</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Northern Estonia under the Swedish crown, Sweden's first Baltic conquest, held from 1561 until Peter the Great took it in the Great Northern War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/terra-mariana">Terra Mariana</a> collapsed under Russian attack, the city of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a> and the knighthoods of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harju-county">Harrien</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/virumaa">Wierland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jarva-county">Jerwen</a> submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-xiv-of-sweden">Eric XIV of Sweden</a> in 1561. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> held on through the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-teusina">Treaty of Teusina</a> in 1595 confirmed its possession of northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The duchy was ruled by a Swedish governor at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a>, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-germans">Baltic German</a> nobility kept wide self-government, their Lutheran church and control of their serfs. Swedish rule founded schools, including a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gymnasium">gymnasium</a> at Reval in 1631, and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> in Estonian; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xi-of-sweden">Charles XI's</a> reduction of noble estates in the 1680s angered the nobles. Reval and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a> were key ports for Baltic trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a> Russian forces took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a> in 1710, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nystad">Treaty of Nystad</a> in 1721 confirmed the loss. The region became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/governorate-of-estonia">Governorate of Estonia</a> within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, its nobles' privileges guaranteed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-estonia-1561-1721.jpg" alt="Duchy of Estonia (1561-1721)" width="320" height="496"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Swedish_Estonia_correct_colours.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1561 CE – 1721 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Reval</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Eric XIV, Gustav II Adolf, Charles XI</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Estonian, Swedish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Swedish Estonia, Estland, Hertigdömet Estland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1641&amp;focus=duchy-of-estonia-1561-1721" aria-label="Duchy of Estonia (1561-1721) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5228 199 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Estonia (1561-1721) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5539 500h0M5381 440h0M5381 440h0M5521 437h0M5521 437h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5548 455h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5548 455h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Estonia. <a href="/atlas?year=1641&amp;focus=duchy-of-estonia-1561-1721">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></d